# React Router Form and HTTPS redirects

Fly terminates TLS at the proxy. Node still sees `request.url` as `http://`. A native `<form method="post">` does a full document POST; if the action then 302s to that `http://` URL, Chrome shows **“The information you’re about to submit is not secure.”**

## Forms

Use React Router `<Form>` (or `useFetcher` / `useSubmit`) for every POST/PATCH/DELETE mutation. Never use a native `<form method="post">`.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — document POST; Chrome warns on HTTPS behind Fly
<form method="post">
  <button type="submit">Samme vare</button>
</form>

// ✅ GOOD — client navigation stays on the HTTPS origin
import { Form } from "react-router";

<Form method="post">
  <button type="submit">Samme vare</button>
</Form>
```

GET search forms may use native `<form method="get">`.

## Redirects after actions

Return a **relative** `Location` with `redirect()` from `react-router`. Do not build an absolute URL from `request.url`.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — Location: http://… behind Fly TLS
return Response.redirect(new URL(`/families/${familyId}/store-mode`, request.url), 302);

// ✅ GOOD — browser resolves against the HTTPS page
import { redirect } from "react-router";

return redirect(`/families/${familyId}/store-mode?${new URLSearchParams({ notice })}`);
```
